<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Varna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1444">1444</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade-of-varna">Crusade of Varna</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varna">Varna</a> was fought on 10 November 1444 near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> port of Varna in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, where the Ottoman army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murad-ii">Murad II</a> defeated a crusading army of Hungarians, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poles">Poles</a> and Wallachians. King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wladyslaw-iii-of-poland">Vladislaus I of Hungary</a> (Władysław III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>) was killed and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-hunyadi">John Hunyadi</a> escaped. The defeat ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade-of-varna">Crusade of Varna</a> and western hopes of driving the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> out of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-varna.jpg" alt="Battle of Varna" width="320" height="198" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan Matejko · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Varna_1444.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
